  "answer": "6",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Plugging in x = 3 gives 0/0. That means 'more work needed', not 'no limit'.",
    "Factor the numerator as a difference of squares."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Direct substitution gives $\\frac{0}{0}$, an indeterminate form.",
    "Factor: $\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{x-3} = x + 3$ for $x \\ne 3$.",
    "The limit only depends on values near 3, so it is $3 + 3 = 6$."
  ],
  "reference": {
